# Build output
build/

# Sony Camera Remote SDK.
#
# Neither the shared libraries nor the headers are committed: the SDK is
# proprietary, licensed by Sony to each developer, and not ours to publish.
# `make sdk` stages both from your own copy of the official package.
lib/
include/CRSDK/
#
# Keep the staged headers to hand when diagnosing camera behaviour. They are the
# authoritative source for property codes, enum values and their semantics -
# three separate faults on 2026-08-16 were only explained by reading them (a
# 1-based caution enum misread as a bitmask, an unread overheating property, an
# unread card-writing state).

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime state (rigd writes these outside the repo, but be explicit)
*.jsonl
.DS_Store

# Software stamp written by deploy/deploy.sh (rig/buildinfo.py --write). It
# describes one deployed tree, so it is never committed.
BUILD_INFO.json

# Vendor documentation trees (1.5 GB, keep local only)
docs/basler-frame-grabber-documentation-v29-en/
docs/basler-product-documentation-v133-en/

# Linux aarch64 SDK staged for the Pi nodes (make sdk-linux). Same reason as
# lib/: large, binary, proprietary, and staged from your own copy.
lib-linux/
